{"timestamp":"2026-08-17T10:27:39.162Z","ordinal":37345,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a00e33-28bf-7050-b2f6-2b374830398b","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a82e2196d9c8198a3d56f38475f596a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The prototype points to a clean boundary: deactivation is a reversible one-row template state change, not a bulk occurrence mutation, so it should preserve every existing flight and booking and stay separate from #85’s broader audit system. The critical detail is race safety—manual and automatic generators must re-check the active state under the same schedule lock, otherwise an in-flight generator can create an occurrence after deactivation commits."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1786962457467,"completed_at_ms":1786962459162}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-17T10:27:39.168Z","ordinal":37346,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a82e2196d9c8198a3d56f38475f596a","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The prototype points to a clean boundary: deactivation is a reversible one-row template state change, not a bulk occurrence mutation, so it should preserve every existing flight and booking and stay separate from #85’s broader audit system. The critical detail is race safety—manual and automatic generators must re-check the active state under the same schedule lock, otherwise an in-flight generator can create an occurrence after deactivation commits."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a00e33-28bf-7050-b2f6-2b374830398b"}}}
