{"timestamp":"2026-08-17T11:06:58.913Z","ordinal":38057,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a00f67-3be1-7b23-9064-bd635ca33aa5","author":"/root/ui_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/ui_review\nPayload:\nRendered UI review is blocked; no browser pass was performed.\n\nBlocker:\n\n- The scratch-database creation hung before output.\n- Docker service inspection requires daemon permission.\n- The escalated `docker compose up -d db` request was interrupted after roughly 21 seconds.\n- Continuing would require repeating the same blocked approval mechanism, which the re-hand explicitly forbids.\n\nCleanup/integrity:\n\n- No dev server, Playwright, Chromium, or database-fixture process survives.\n- No issue #83 screenshots were created.\n- No fixture data was created by the browser harness.\n- The interrupted Docker command may have started the repository database service; its state cannot be confirmed without the same blocked daemon permission.\n- Worktree remains exactly 12 modified + 5 untracked intended paths, with no staged or committed `main...HEAD` diff.\n- `git diff --check` is clean; no source/status-reported file changed.\n\nSource inspection confirms a likely rendered focus defect requiring live verification once PostgreSQL is available: [FlightScheduleActivationForm.tsx](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/components/ui/FlightScheduleActivationForm.tsx:94) focuses `.schedule-activation-success`, while [globals.css](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/app/globals.css:1447) styles only `.schedule-terms-success:focus`. This is source-level evidence only, not a completed rendered finding."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a00e33-28bf-7050-b2f6-2b374830398b"}}}
