{"timestamp":"2026-08-17T11:30:17.484Z","ordinal":38290,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a00f7c-930c-7a62-89b3-91b225c1fed1","author":"/root/verifier","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/verifier\nPayload:\nVerification completed, but the slice is not ready to pass.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. Regression/blocker — deactivation is not serialized with either occurrence generator. [flightScheduleActivationService.ts](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/lib/flightScheduleActivationService.ts:40) locks the schedule, but automatic generation reads active templates without that lock at [FlightScheduleService.ts](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/lib/FlightScheduleService.ts:75), and manual generation reads once at [actions.ts](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/app/actions.ts:1336) before creating flights later at line 1414. A generator can read `isActive=true`, deactivation can commit, and the generator can then create an occurrence after the operator received success. This contradicts the primary “stops automatic and manual generation” contract.\n\n2. Coverage gap — mutant 1 only proves that some `$queryRaw` call occurs. The unit assertion at [flightScheduleActivationService.test.ts](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/__tests__/lib/flightScheduleActivationService.test.ts:34) does not constrain `FOR UPDATE`, and the database test is sequential. Removing only `FOR UPDATE` would survive. A deterministic contention test and shared generator/deactivation locking contract are needed.\n\n3. Coverage gap — the new `flightScheduleActivationSchema` validation-failure branch has no direct test or reported mutant. No test submits a non-positive schedule ID or non-boolean state and proves rejection before the service.\n\nAll 19 reported mutant claims were otherwise auditable and correctly selected. Rows 2–19 constrain idempotency, scoped counts, staff access, typed errors, inactive generation gates, page projection, UI state/focus, server-recount truthfulness, and runtime focus styling.\n\nExecutable results:\n\n- TypeScript: passed.\n- Lint: 0 errors, same 8 baseline warnings.\n- Unit project: passed.\n- Database project: passed, including the new activation database suite.\n- Build and standalone sanitizer: passed.\n- Playwright: 42/42 passed in 5.2 minutes.\n- Three non-failing disruption `ECONNRESET` diagnostics recurred; no retry or test failure.\n\nMigration proof, dependency audit, and container scan were correctly skipped: no migration/schema, dependency, or image/sanitizer source changed.\n\nFinal integrity: exactly 13 modified and 5 untracked intended files remain; no staged/committed diff, `git diff --check` passed, `.next` and Playwright artifacts removed, port 3000 free, and no verifier server/process remains."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a00e33-28bf-7050-b2f6-2b374830398b"}}}
