{"timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:04:12.199Z","ordinal":38894,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a00f9b-9f26-7e50-bc5c-6362710d6558","author":"/root/verifier","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/verifier\nPayload:\nVerifier result: executable gates pass, with two actionable coverage findings.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. The shared advisory lock’s lifetime is not behaviorally selected. Current database races manually hold `lockFlightScheduleGenerationState`; they do not prove that `withFlightScheduleGenerationLock` keeps the lock until its callback finishes. Acquiring/committing the lock in one transaction and running the operation in another would leave the current tests and mutants green while reintroducing activation/generation overlap. Add a deterministic helper-level contention test.\n\n2. `FOR UPDATE` is checked only through `rowLockSql.join('?').toContain('FOR UPDATE')`. Moving that token into a SQL comment would preserve the assertion while removing the actual row lock. No database test contends a direct schedule update/delete against activation. Add a real PostgreSQL lock-timeout contention test.\n\nChecks:\n\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: pass.\n- `npm run lint`: pass, 0 errors and the same 8 baseline warnings.\n- `npm run test:unit`: pass, 83 suites / 932 tests. Existing non-failing React `act(...)` warnings appeared.\n- `npm run test:database`: permitted rerun pass, 39 suites / 291 tests. Initial sandbox run failed uniformly because localhost PostgreSQL was inaccessible; expected negative-path Prisma logs appeared on the green run.\n- `npm run build`: permitted rerun pass; sanitizer removed one standalone environment file. Initial sandbox run hit Turbopack’s process/port restriction.\n- `npx playwright test`: pass, 42/42 in 5.6 minutes with clean teardown; recurring `NO_COLOR` warnings only.\n- No retries exposed a product flake.\n\nMutant audit:\n\n- All 30 reported edits are restored and their stated focused assertions select the edited values or branches.\n- Rows 20–30 close the original stale-candidate, missing validation, and missing shared-lock invocation findings.\n- Row 24’s `pg_blocking_pids` test is deterministic and removes timing dependence.\n- Selection remains incomplete specifically for whole-callback advisory-lock lifetime and real `FOR UPDATE` semantics, as above.\n\nSkips:\n\n- Migration proof: not reachable; no schema or migration changes.\n- Production dependency audit: not reachable; package files unchanged.\n- Container scan/probes: not reachable; Dockerfile, standalone sanitizer, and image paths unchanged.\n\nIntegrity:\n\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n- Status remains exactly 15 modified and 6 intended untracked files.\n- Generated `.next`, `test-results`, and `playwright-report` artifacts removed.\n- No Jest, Playwright, or Next server remains; port 3000 is free.\n- No scratch database was created."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a00e33-28bf-7050-b2f6-2b374830398b"}}}
