{"timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:16:42.733Z","ordinal":38990,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a00fa7-12ed-7870-aa81-8bad8fff3468","call_id":"call_PIO2sQJZoWbWn0weGZAGPmhR","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/ui_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Browser plugin tools were absent; I used the mandated throwaway Playwright fallback.\\n\\nNo actionable UI findings.\\n\\nPassed at 390x844, 768x1024, and 1440x900:\\n\\n- Active/inactive status and preservation copy were truthful.\\n- Legacy Delete control was absent.\\n- Keyboard confirmation and submit worked.\\n- Pending controls retained visible focus, remained natively enabled, and exposed `aria-disabled=\\\"true\\\"` plus `aria-busy=\\\"true\\\"`.\\n- Duplicate activation generated no second action request.\\n- Deactivation and reactivation statuses owned focus with the exact 3px solid amber outline, 3px offset, and 5px halo.\\n- Two linked occurrences and the booking itinerary remained unchanged through both transitions.\\n- Inactive schedule disappeared from the manual generator and returned after reactivation.\\n- Safe not-found error showed only `This flight schedule no longer exists.`, owned focus, and received the same amber treatment.\\n- No horizontal document overflow or HTTP 500s.\\n\\nPhone and desktop diagnostics were clean. Tablet recorded two `ERR_ABORTED` header POSTs only when the throwaway harness navigated immediately after refresh; all product assertions had passed, and the same route completed cleanly once post-refresh requests were allowed to settle. This was classified as harness navigation cancellation, not an application failure.\\n\\nTwenty-one screenshots are under [test-results/ui-review](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review), named `issue83-schedule-activation-{viewport}-{state}.png`.\\n\\nAll fixtures were removed, the exact disposable database was dropped, the dev server stopped, and port 3000 is clear. Worktree remains exactly 13 modified + 5 untracked intended paths, with no staged or committed `main...HEAD` diff; `git diff --check` is clean. No source/status-reported file changed.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/verifier\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a00e33-28bf-7050-b2f6-2b374830398b"}}}
