{"timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:35:12.403Z","ordinal":39217,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_00fb20eee1c75140016a82fffa8a44819883ff916a11ead3f6","status":"completed","call_id":"call_7yjlM5CK1GDHsAJVZ9LC7qWx","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /tmp/travel-app-pr83-body.md\\n+## Summary\\n+\\n+- add a reversible staff workflow to deactivate or reactivate a flight schedule from its impact preview\\n+- keep linked occurrences and bookings unchanged while removing inactive templates from automatic and manual generation\\n+- serialize every generator with activation changes so stale reads cannot create inventory after deactivation succeeds\\n+- preserve concurrent-create recovery after PostgreSQL aborts a failed generation transaction\\n+\\n+## Why\\n+\\n+Issue #83 requires safe schedule lifecycle behavior without silently orphaning or rewriting booked flights. This is the smallest independently shippable slice: deactivation changes only the template state, uses the existing impact preview as its confirmation surface, preserves history, and can be retried safely. Permanent deletion remains a later slice.\\n+\\n+## Validation\\n+\\n+- rendered UI review at 390x844, 768x1024, and 1440x900\\n+- `npx tsc --noEmit`\\n+- `npm run lint` (0 errors; 8 baseline warnings)\\n+- `npm run test:unit` (83 suites, 933 tests)\\n+- `npm run test:database` (39 suites, 293 tests)\\n+- `npm run build`\\n+- `npx playwright test` (42/42)\\n+- 34 focused mutation checks audited by the verifier\\n+\\n+Part of #83.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a00e33-28bf-7050-b2f6-2b374830398b"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-17T12:35:12.741Z","ordinal":39218,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a00e33-28bf-7050-b2f6-2b374830398b","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-d3667e83-fe0d-4b42-8f29-31a658431f89","changes":{"/tmp/travel-app-pr83-body.md":{"type":"add","content":"## Summary\n\n- add a reversible staff workflow to deactivate or reactivate a flight schedule from its impact preview\n- keep linked occurrences and bookings unchanged while removing inactive templates from automatic and manual generation\n- serialize every generator with activation changes so stale reads cannot create inventory after deactivation succeeds\n- preserve concurrent-create recovery after PostgreSQL aborts a failed generation transaction\n\n## Why\n\nIssue #83 requires safe schedule lifecycle behavior without silently orphaning or rewriting booked flights. This is the smallest independently shippable slice: deactivation changes only the template state, uses the existing impact preview as its confirmation surface, preserves history, and can be retried safely. Permanent deletion remains a later slice.\n\n## Validation\n\n- rendered UI review at 390x844, 768x1024, and 1440x900\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`\n- `npm run lint` (0 errors; 8 baseline warnings)\n- `npm run test:unit` (83 suites, 933 tests)\n- `npm run test:database` (39 suites, 293 tests)\n- `npm run build`\n- `npx playwright test` (42/42)\n- 34 focused mutation checks audited by the verifier\n\nPart of #83.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /tmp/travel-app-pr83-body.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1786970112500,"completed_at_ms":1786970112741}}
